    {
      "slug": "supers-as-combat-states",
      "title": "Supers as Combat States",
      "creator": "GuardianDesign",
      "type": "design",
      "categories": [
        "gameplay",
        "abilities"
      ],
      "status": "direction",
      "date": "2026-04-27",
      "updated": "2026-05-18",
      "featured": true,
      "question": "what-should-supers-become",
      "summary": "Transform Supers from one-time attacks into sustained, expressive combat states that change how you play, not just what you do.",
      "cover": {
        "type": "image",
        "media": "/media/concepts/c2.jpg",
        "thumbnail": "/media/concepts/c2.jpg"
      },
      "tools": [
        "Unreal",
        "After Effects"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "heading": "The idea",
          "text": "Instead of pressing a button for one oversized attack, activating a Super should transition you into a temporary combat state with an altered moveset, different movement, and new decisions to make.\n\nThe Super stops being the attack. It becomes the twenty seconds you spend deciding how to spend it."
        },
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "heading": "The proposal",
          "steps": [
            "Normal State \u2014 Build energy through combat and abilities",
            "Super Activation \u2014 Enter a transformed combat state",
            "Altered Moveset \u2014 New abilities, effects, and playstyle",
            "Exit & Opportunity \u2014 State ends with a finisher or teamwork window"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "heading": "Why this matters",
          "items": [
            "More room for player expression",
            "Buildcrafting continues inside the Super",
            "Fireteams can combine states deliberately",
            "Duration replaces burst as the balancing lever"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "A Super should change what you can do, not just what you press."
        }
      ],
      "takeaways": [
        "Supers become a gameplay state, not a stronger ability",
        "Decision making continues for the whole duration",
        "Weapons stay relevant inside the state",
        "Exotics get somewhere new to modify"
      ],
